ercentage-criteria-for-the-HS-First-Year-Examination-2026\nMerit List : B.A. 1st Semester (FYUGP), 2025\nFirst Merit List for admission into B.A. 1st Semester (FYUGP), 2025\nSecond Merit List for Admission into BA 1st Semester (FYUGP), 2025\nSituation Vacant\nInterview for the post of Assistant Professor in the Department of English\nWelcome to UMK College\nVision and Mission\nPage 1 of 2\n1\n2\nAffidavit Registration Form For Anti Ragging\nAnti Ragging Complaint Registration\nCollege Notice\nNOTICE INVITING QUOTATIONS (NIQ) FOR METERIALS\nNOTICE INVITING QUOTATIONS (NIQ) FOR METERIALS\nAdmission Open for H.S. 1st Year, 2026-27\n1st Merit list\n1st Merit list HS 1st Year for Admission, 2026-27\nNOTICE INVITING QUOTATIONS (NIQ) FOR METERIALS\nNOTICE INVITING QUOTATIONS (NIQ) FOR METERIALS\nAdmission Open for H.S. 1st Year, 2026-27\n1st Merit list\n1st Merit list HS 1st Year for Admission, 2026-27\nPast Notices\nUMKC Archive\nApril, 2025\nDecember, 2024\nJuly, 2024\nJune, 2024\nMay, 2024\nFebruary, 2024\nJuly, 2023\nJanuary, 2023\nDecember, 2022\nNovember, 2022\nOctober, 2022\nAugust, 2022\nJuly, 2022\nMarch, 2022\nPrincipal\nWelcome Message from the Principal of Ujani Majuli Kherkatia College\nIt gives me immense pleasure to welcome you to Ujani Majuli Kherkatia College, an institution that has been dedicated to the cause of higher education and human development since its establishment in 1973. Over the past five decades, the college has witnessed continuous growth and transformation, earning recognition as one of the leading institutions of higher learning in the region. Through its unwavering commitment to academic excellence, moral values, and holistic education, the college has become a preferred destination for aspiring learners.\nEducation, in its truest sense, is not merely the transmission of knowledge but the awakening of curiosity, creativity, and the spirit of inquiry. The teaching profession carries the noble responsibility of inspiring young minds to think critically, learn continuously, and contribute meaningfully to society. At our institution, teachers strive not only to impart knowledge but also to nurture intellectual growth, scientific temperament, ethical values, and a sense of national responsibility among students. We firmly believe that true education equips learners with the wisdom to apply knowledge constructively and the confidence to face the challenges of an ever-changing world.\nThe essence of quality education lies in continuous growth and adaptation. In a rapidly evolving global society, educators and learners alike must remain receptive to new ideas, innovative methods of learning, and emerging perspectives in various fields of knowledge. An educated individual with an integrated personality is capable not only of achieving personal success but also of serving humanity with integrity, compassion, and courage. The highest virtue of education is to inspire individuals to become socially responsible citizens who contribute positively towards the welfare of society.\nThe tradition of Ujani Majuli Kherkatia College harmoniously combines academic excellence with a vibrant co-curricular environment encompassing sports, cultural activities, leadership training, and community engagement programmes. Our mission is to cultivate in students a lifelong love for learning and to develop the skills, values, and attitudes essential for becoming responsible global citizens. We endeavour to empower our students with resilience, confidence, optimism, and the ability to adapt successfully to future challenges. Simultaneously, we strive to inculcate the values of mutual respect, trust, discipline, and cooperation, which form the foundation of meaningful relationships and lasting success.\nAt Ujani Majuli Kherkatia College, we firmly believe that education is a holistic process aimed at the all-round development of an individual. Guided by the spirit of belongingness and collective responsibility, the institution regards itself as a nurturing academic family dedicated to the intellectual, emotional, moral, and social development of every learner. The healthy academic environment, rich cultural heritage, disciplined atmosphere, and student-centric approach of the college inspire learners to realise their fullest potential and prepare them to face the complexities and challenges of life with confidence and determination.\nI warmly welcome all students, parents, guardians, and well-wishers to this esteemed institution. I also take this opportunity to express my sincere gratitude to everyone associated with the college for becoming our valued partners in the noble mission of education, inspiring lives, and shaping futures.\nDr. Jahnabee Lahkar Boruah\nPrincipal\nUjani Majuli Kherkatia College, Majuli\nAccess Institutional e-Mail\nUser Login\nUsername\nShow\nRemember Me\nLog in\nForgot your username?\nForgot your password?\nYou are here:\nHome\nDownloads\nDefence Drone and Artificial Intelligence Workshop ( April - May ) Updates\nDef-Space Workshop April\nLYNHDOH COMMITTEE REPORT\nB.A. Course Syllabus:\nAssamese (Honours):\nSyllabus\n&\nCourse Structure\nAssamese (Non Honours):\nSyllabus\n&\nCourse Structure\nEconomics:\nHonours\n&\nNon-Honours\nEducation:\nHonours\n&\nNon-Honours\nEnglish:\nAECC\n,\nHonours\n,\nSem-I writing Skills\n,\nAlt-Non-Honours\nHistory:\nHonours\n&\nNon-Honours\nSociology:\nHonours & Non-Honours\nPol. Science:\nHonours\n&\nNon-Honours\nSocial Media Link:\nFacebook Page\nFacebook\nFacebook Fan Page\nX (Twiter)\nAll India Survey on Higher Education (AISHE), 2023-24\nCertificate\nDCF\nTIF\nNIRF, 2025\nDibrugarh University Annual Reports\n2023\nOthers:\nTHE BHARATIYA NYAYA SANHITA\nMajuli E-magazine\nUseful Links\nUGC\nDST\nNMEICT\nAssam Govt.\nNATS\nNational Academic Depository\nNational Digital Library\nDibrugarh University\nGauhati\nUniversity\nAssam University\nVOTERS' SERVICE PORTAL\nVoter Helpline App\nOur Address\nUjani Majuli Kherkatia College\nP.O. Rata